ality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title presents a generative foundation model for multimodal histopathology, and the abstract mentions natural language prompts. This supports a substantive bio-plus-text model rather than a wrapper.","evidence_snippet":"“A Generative Foundation Model for Multimodal Histopathology” and “natural language prompts”"},{"record_id":"rec_003853","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title suggests an AI systems paper, but the provided abstract text is too fragmentary to establish whether it is a primary model paper or a review-style piece. The text-bio modeling details are not clear from the snippet.","evidence_snippet":"“From Modality Translation to Regulatory Reasoning: Interpretable AI for Single-Cell Multi-Omic Systems” with only fragmentary abstract text"},{"record_id":"rec_003854","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary spatial multi-modal omics method paper, but the abstract contains no substantive text or language component. It focuses on gene expression, protein abundance, chromatin accessibility, and graph learning.","evidence_snippet":"“Spatial multi-modal omics technologies” and “adaptive graph learning for spatial multi-modal omics analysis”"},{"record_id":"rec_003855","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The venue and framing indicate a review article on a broad topic rather than a primary model paper. The abstract fragment is about advancing single-cell omics and therapeutics with quantum computing.","evidence_snippet":"Title/venue framing: “Nature Reviews Molecular …” and “Advancing single-cell omics and cell-based therapeutics with quantum computing”"},{"record_id":"rec_003856","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title describes a biologically informed dual-branch transformer for drug-induced cellular perturbation responses, which is a primary model paper. The abstract fragment also references single-cell large language model architectures and NLP-style tokens.","evidence_snippet":"“biologically informed dual-branch transformer” and “single-cell large language models” / “word tokens in natural language processing”"}]}
