_rationale":"The venue and framing indicate a review article on a broad topic rather than a primary model paper. The abstract fragment is about advancing single-cell omics and therapeutics with quantum computing.","evidence_snippet":"Title/venue framing: “Nature Reviews Molecular …” and “Advancing single-cell omics and cell-based therapeutics with quantum computing”"},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003855","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title indicates a review-style article on single-cell omics and therapeutics rather than a primary model paper. The snippet is too incomplete to establish a specific generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Advancing single-cell omics and cell-based therapeutics with quantum computing\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"review_editorial","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear"}}},{"record_id":"rec_003857","title":"AI-powered Immune Cell Knowledge Graph (ICKG) with granular immune contexts enables immune program interpretation","abstract":"Abstract\n                  \n                    The widespread application of single-cell and spatial omics to models and patient samples has transformed immune cell profiling across physiological conditions. However, knowledge of immune cell states, functions, and gene regulation remains fragmented across publications, limiting our ability to synthesize insights and derive mechanistic understanding from the literature. To address this gap and facilitate literature integration, we constructed Immune Cell Knowledge Graphs (ICKGs)—four cell type-specific graphs derived from over 24,000 cancer immunotherapy-focused PubMed abstracts using large language models (LLMs) with “human verifiable” validation. Unlike conventional databases, which provide context-agnostic pathways, ICKGs capture directed, literature-supported relationships among genes, pathways and immune functions, enabling context-aware reasoning. We validated ICKGs using perturbation datasets from cytokine stimulation and CRISPR experiments, demonstrating that ICKGs contain more accurate and immunologically coherent contexts than canonical databases. As a key application, ICKGs provide interpretable and accurate pathway annotations, including signatures unannotated by canonical databases or used in immuno-oncology. To support community use, we created an interactive portal (\n                    https://kchen-lab.github.io/immune-knowledgegraph.github.io/\n                    ) to perform ICKG-based pathway annotations, allowing researchers to explore immune cell-specific insights grounded in literature. This work establishes ICKGs as a scalable framework for immune-specific functional interpretation and mechanistic hypothesis generation in single-cell and spatial omics.","doi":"","year":"2026","venue":"npj Artificial …","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003857","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes construction of Immune Cell Knowledge Graphs from PubMed abstracts with LLMs and an interactive portal. This is a resource/database paper, not a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"constructed Immune Cell Knowledge Graphs (ICKGs)... derived from over 24,000... PubMed abstracts using large language models\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003857","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work builds Immune Cell Knowledge Graphs using LLMs over PubMed abstracts; it is a literature-integration/annotation system, not a generative model. The abstract does not describe broad pretraining or a foundation-model-like pretrained architecture.","evidence_snippet":"\"constructed Immune Cell Knowledge Graphs... using large language models (LLMs)\" and \"interactive portal ... to perform ICKG-based pathway annotations\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"benchmark_resource","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_003860","title":"Towards Virtual Cell Construction by AI","abstract":"known biological factors such as cell type, treatment, and tem benchmarking framework  for single-cell disentanglement,  and, where possible, natural language abstractions, I aim to","doi":"","year":"NA","venue":"NA","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003860","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title and fragment read like a perspective or concept piece rather than a concrete model paper. The abstract is too incomplete to establish a substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Towards Virtual Cell Construction by AI\" and \"I aim to\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003860","paper_type":"unclear","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclu