y substantive text component.","evidence_snippet":"\"Foundation model representation ... for spatial gene expression prediction\""},{"record_id":"rec_000256","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract centers on benchmarking 79 large language models across 1130 transcriptomics datasets and releasing a platform. This is primarily a benchmark/resource and application platform paper, not a new candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"systematically benchmarked 79 large language models\" and \"developed AICellType ... a free, open-source R package and web platform\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0170.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001353","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a prognostic test that extracts features from an existing vision transformer foundation model and combines them with clinical data. It does not describe a generative architecture.","evidence_snippet":"“utilized a vision transformer pan-cancer foundation model trained with self-supervised learning to extract features”"},{"record_id":"rec_001354","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic review of AI studies, not a primary model paper. The abstract summarizes literature on diagnosis performance rather than proposing a generative model.","evidence_snippet":"“systematically evaluate the diagnostic performance of artificial intelligence” and “A total of 44 studies met the inclusion criteria”"},{"record_id":"rec_001355","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The method uses CNN, self-attention, LSTM, and GNN for prediction and classification. No generative mechanism or foundation-model-style pretraining is described.","evidence_snippet":"“gene expression prediction” and “regulatory element classification tasks”"},{"record_id":"rec_001356","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"SeqMate is a pipeline that uses a large language model to automate RNA-seq analysis and generate written reports. The abstract does not give enough detail about the underlying model’s pretraining or foundation-model characteristics.","evidence_snippet":"“utilizing the power of a large language model (LLM)” and “producing written reports”"},{"record_id":"rec_001357","paper_type":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is about whole-genome sequencing and bioinformatics annotation of a bacterial isolate. It does not describe any generative model or foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“Whole genome sequencing emerged as the methodological linchpin” and “bioinformatics analysis”"},{"record_id":"rec_001358","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a parameter-efficient fine-tuning framework built on existing single-cell large language models. The abstract explicitly references broad zero-shot use and adapting a frozen backbone rather than introducing a new base model.","evidence_snippet":"“single-cell large language models (scLLMs)” and “freezing the backbone model and updating only the adapter parameters”"},{"record_id":"rec_001359","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"NicheTrans is presented as a Transformer-based cross-omics translation framework, but the abstract does not explicitly state a decoder, autoregressive, or seq2seq generative mechanism. It also does not provide evidence of broad pretraining or foundation-model-like scope.","evidence_snippet":"“first, spatially-aware cross-omics translation method” and “Transformer-based multi-modal deep learning framework”"},{"record_id":"rec_001360","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of AI applications in pulmonary medicine, not a primary model paper. The abstract surveys computer vision, predictive modeling, and COVID-19 applications rather than describing a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“The goal of this review is to provide pulmonary specialists” and “we review some of the literature”"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0482.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_003849","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a unified zero-shot inference framework for existing single-cell foundation models, not a new generative model. The abstract focuses on preprocessing, tokenization, and distributed inference.","evidence_snippet":"\"introduce scUnify, a unified zero-shot inference framework for single-cell foundation models\" and \"automatically manages environment isolation, preprocessing, and tokenization\""},{"record_id":"rec_003850","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The paper evaluates existing single-cell large language models rather than introducing a new model. It clearly discusses large-scale pretraining and task transfer, but the abstract does not explicitly establish a generative architecture.","evidence_snippet":"\"systematically evaluate two representative scFMs, Geneformer and scGPT\" and \"benefits of large-scale pretraining\""},{"record_id":"rec_003851","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a manually annotated corpus and text-mining resource, not a generative model paper. The abstract describes NER, entity linking, and ontology expansion.","evidence_snippet":"\"manually annotated collection\" and \"embedding-based approaches support zero-shot entity linking\""},{"record_id":"rec_003852","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes"