es","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SeqMate wraps an existing LLM to automate RNA-seq workflows and generate written reports. The LLM is used as an interface/reporting layer rather than a substantive text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"utilizing the power of a large language model (LLM) to automate both data preparation and analysis\"; \"producing written reports\""},{"record_id":"rec_001357","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a whole-genome sequencing and annotation study, not a candidate generative model paper. No substantive text or language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"\"Whole Genome Sequencing of Enterococcus faecalis\"; \"gene annotation\""},{"record_id":"rec_001358","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This presents a parameter-efficient fine-tuning framework for single-cell large language models. The abstract clearly links the text/modeling component to biological single-cell data and downstream cell-state tasks.","evidence_snippet":"\"single-cell large language models (scLLMs)\"; \"parameter-efficient fine-tuning (scPEFT) framework\""},{"record_id":"rec_001359","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"NicheTrans is a transformer-based multi-modal framework for spatial omics translation. The abstract does not describe a substantive text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"spatially-aware cross-omics translation method\"; \"Transformer-based multi-modal deep learning framework\""},{"record_id":"rec_001360","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This paper is explicitly a review of AI in pulmonary medicine. It discusses applications and limitations rather than introducing a new text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"The goal of this review is to provide pulmonary specialists... information pertinent to the use of AI\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0054.stderr.log:1270:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0208.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001657","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Abstract frames the work as benchmarking BCR sequencing technologies and explicitly says it generates a resource for the community. It is about immune repertoire sequencing, not a text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“benchmarking experiment” and “generated a resource for the immunology community”"},{"record_id":"rec_001658","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a Comment that discusses the landscape and barriers around single-cell large language models rather than presenting a new model. It mentions biomedical single-cell omics and LLMs, but not a specific primary text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“In this Comment, we examine the current landscape of scLLMs”"},{"record_id":"rec_001659","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_component_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract reads as a forward-looking commentary on virtual cells, organs, and foundation models rather than a primary model paper. It does not clearly specify a substantive text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"“Navigating the Deep Waters of Medical AI Models” and “Ultimately, the trajectory...”"},{"record_id":"rec_001660","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This presents a new generative self-expression model for single-cell and spatial multimodal data. The abstract describes omics integration and representation learning, but no substantive text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"“we propose a contrastive and generative deep self-expression model” for “single-cell and spatial multimodal data”"},{"record_id":"rec_001661","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work reuses pre-trained DNA language models and compares embedding-based pipelines versus fine-tuning for downstream genomic prediction. That is an application of existing models, not a new substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“Large pre-trained DNA language models” and “embedding-based pipelines”"},{"record_id":"rec_001662","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"FEDKEA integrates a pretrained protein language model with KNN for enzyme annotation, which is a downstream application pipeline around existing model embeddings. The abstract does not support a new text-bio foundation model with a substantive bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“integrates ESM-2 and distance-weighted KNN” for “enzyme function annotation”"},{"record_id":"rec_001663","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a genomic data compression/encoding paper, not a generative text-bio model paper. The abstract describes direct coding of DNA bases and does not mention any text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"“two-bit coding” for “genomic sequence” compression"},{"record_id":"rec_001664","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this review synthesizes the technology and applications of droplet-based scRNA-seq. It is a review, not a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“This review synthesizes the technological evolution” of droplet-based single-cell RNA sequencing"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0166.stderr.log:519:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0482.stderr.log:108:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_003849","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"A unified zero-shot inference framework for existing single-cell foundation models, not a new candidate model. The abstract focuses on environment isolation, preprocessing, tokenization, and benchmarking of model embeddings.","evidence_snippet":"“unified zero-shot inference framework for single-cell foundation models” and “manages environment isolation, preprocessing, and tokenization”"},{"record_id":"rec_003850","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an evaluation study of existing single-cell large language models across tasks, rather than a new model paper. It benchmarks Geneformer and scGPT on perturbation prediction and cell type annotation.","evidence_snippet":"“systematically evaluate two representative scFMs, Geneformer and scGPT” across tasks"},{"record_id":"rec_003851","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a manually annotated text corpus and text mining utilities, not a new generative model. It links literature mentions of cell phenotypes to Cell Ontology terms.","evidence_snippet":"“manually annotated collection” and “fine-tuning transformer-based models on CellLink”"},{"record_id":"rec_003852","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title presents a generative foundation model for multimodal histopathology, and the abstract mentions natural language prompts. This supports a substantive bio-plus-text model rather than a wrapper.","evidence_snippet":"“A Generative Foundation Model for Multimodal Histopathology” and “natural language prompts”"},{"record_id":"rec_003853","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title suggests an AI systems paper, but the provided abstract text is too fragmentary to establish whether it is a primary model paper or a review-style piece. The text-bio modeling details are not clear from the snippet.","evidence_snippet":"“From Modality Translation to Regulatory Reasoning: Interpretable AI for Single-Cell Multi-Omic Systems” with only fragmentary abstract text"},{"record_id":"rec_003854","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary spatial multi-modal omics method paper, but the abstract contains no substantive text or language component. It focuses on gene expression, protein abundance, chromatin accessibility, and graph learning.","evidence_snippet":"“Spatial multi-modal omics technologies” and “adaptive graph learning for spatial multi-modal omics analysis”"},{"record_id":"rec_003855","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The venue and framing indicate a review article on a broad topic rather than a primary model paper. The abstract fragment is about advancing single-cell omics and therapeutics with quantum computing.","evidence_snippet":"Title/venue framing: “Nature Reviews Molecular …” and “Advancing single-cell omics and cell-based therapeutics with quantum computing”"},{"record_id":"rec_003856","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title describes a biologically informed dual-branch transformer for drug-induced cellular perturbation responses, which is a primary model paper. The abstract fragment also references single-cell large language model architectures and NLP-style tokens.","evidence_snippet":"“biologically informed dual-branch transformer” and “single-cell large language models” / “word tokens in natural language processing”"}]}
