ent is about advancing single-cell omics and therapeutics with quantum computing.","evidence_snippet":"Title/venue framing: “Nature Reviews Molecular …” and “Advancing single-cell omics and cell-based therapeutics with quantum computing”"},{"record_id":"rec_003856","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title describes a biologically informed dual-branch transformer for drug-induced cellular perturbation responses, which is a primary model paper. The abstract fragment also references single-cell large language model architectures and NLP-style tokens.","evidence_snippet":"“biologically informed dual-branch transformer” and “single-cell large language models” / “word tokens in natural language processing”"}]}
